WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.919
that got me thinking about an article
that I read about Anthony Bourdain and

00:00:06.919 --> 00:00:15.690
Anthony Bourdain obviously he was about
as successful as as anyone could be I

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:23.400
mean he was a successful guy in so many
aspects and yet and yet he killed

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:32.550
himself and I didn't know him personally
but you know he knew people that I know

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:37.260
you know he was he was friends with Joe
Rogan he was he was friends with Harley

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:49.500
Flanagan he was friends with guys that
guys that have really good guys and so

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:55.730
in that way I kind of felt like I knew
what kind of a guy he was at least and

00:00:55.730 --> 00:01:01.500
even from the outside even without
having any connections to him at all he

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.869
was the kind of guy that had just about
everything that that that most people

00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:22.049
would want and even still I mean
obviously that wasn't enough well in the

00:01:22.049 --> 00:01:27.119
article that I read there was a quote
from one of Anthony Bourdain's books and

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:36.770
the book was called a Cook's Tour he
said in this book I wanted adventures I

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:44.850
wanted to go up the num river to the
heart of darkness in Cambodia I wanted

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:51.740
to ride out into a desert on Camelback
sand and dunes in every direction

00:01:51.740 --> 00:02:00.329
eat whole roasted lamb with my fingers I
wanted to kick snow off my boots in a

00:02:00.329 --> 00:02:05.689
Mafia nightclub in Russia I wanted to
play with automatic weapons in pnom pen

00:02:05.689 --> 00:02:11.149
recapture the past in a small boy stur
village in France

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:20.730
step into a CD neon-lit boqueria in
rural Mexico I wanted to run roadblocks

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:26.340
in the middle of the night blowing past
angry militia with a handful of hurled

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:37.230
marlboro packs experience fear
excitement wonder I wanted kicks the

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:45.569
kind of melodramatic thrills and chills
I'd yearned for since childhood the kind

00:02:45.569 --> 00:02:52.190
of adventure I'd found as a little boy
in the pages of my Tintin comic books I

00:02:52.190 --> 00:03:05.430
wanted to see the world and I wanted the
world to be just like the movies that's

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:21.600
what Anthony Bourdain said just like the
movies but you know what to me the world

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:37.670
is not like the movies the movies aren't
real they don't exist but you do and

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:44.370
life this life is it's better than any
movie there is movies are supposed to

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:52.829
provoke emotion they're supposed to make
you feel something but I have a better

00:03:52.829 --> 00:04:05.790
idea go out into the world and actually
feel it go feel joy and love and triumph

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:18.829
and rapture and ecstasy and glory go
feel those things and you know with

00:04:18.829 --> 00:04:27.289
those feelings there will be other
feelings as well there'll be sorrow and

00:04:27.289 --> 00:04:39.050
pain and sadness and desolation and
suffering there'll be all those feelings

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:54.289
too but you know what that's okay that's
okay take both sides feel all of it

00:04:54.289 --> 00:05:03.620
that's what life is those feelings those
emotions those eyes and those lows those

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:13.000
are life and those emotions and those
feelings are better than any movie

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:17.440
because they are real

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:32.120
so make your own comic book make your
life your own movie but actually make it

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:41.360
better than a movie not not better
because it's more adventurous or more

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:53.900
romantic or more melodramatic make it
better because it's real it's real so it

00:05:53.900 --> 00:06:03.620
is better and you know what real comes
with some downsides real comes with some

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:06.159
darkness

00:06:12.649 --> 00:06:23.669
but that's okay it's okay because when
you know the darkness the light becomes

00:06:23.669 --> 00:06:38.689
even brighter so go out there move
toward the light move toward the light

00:06:39.589 --> 00:06:48.319
and live live

